    <string name="advice_title">💡 Recommended voltages for your battery</string>
    <string name="advice_body">BMS protection: %1$.3f V per cell × %2$d = %3$.2f V. The BMS cuts charging there.

• Charger: set it to %4$.1f V (%5$.2f V per cell) so the charge ends just below the protection and the BMS does not have to stop it.
• Full-charge alarm: %6$.1f V (%7$.2f V per cell) — reachable, and rings just before the charge ends.</string>
    <string name="advice_current_unreachable">Your current alarm voltage (%1$.1f V) is above the BMS protection, so it can never ring.</string>
